.TH MPV-MUSIC 1 "November 2026" "mpv-music 0.30.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mpv-music \- terminal-native music player and library browser for mpv
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mpv-music
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fITARGET\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mpv-music
is a terminal-native music player and library browser written in Rust that wraps
.BR mpv (1)
with fast metadata indexing, fuzzy search (powered by skim), rich previews,
YouTube search/streaming via
.BR yt-dlp (1),
and curated internet radio stations.
.PP
When invoked with no arguments,
.B mpv-music
launches the interactive Main Menu TUI. When given a
.IR TARGET ,
it either plays a matching local file, directory, or URL directly, or runs a
unified fuzzy search across Track Title, Artist, and Album.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Library & Indexing"
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-refresh\-index
Update the music index incrementally, detecting new, modified, or removed files.
.TP
.B \-\-reindex
Force a full rescan of all configured music directories.
.TP
.BI \-\-add\-dir " PATH..."
Add one or more directories to
.I music_dirs
in
.I config.toml
and refresh the index.
.TP
.BI \-\-remove\-dir " PATH..." "\fR, \fP" \-\-rm\-dir " PATH..."
Remove one or more directories from
.IR music_dirs .
.TP
.B \-\-manage\-dirs
Open the Interactive Directory Manager.
.TP
.BI \-e ", " \-\-ext " EXT1,EXT2"
Override allowed file extensions for the current session.
.TP
.B \-\-serial
Force single-threaded (serial) indexing and processing.
.SS "Filtering & Search"
.TP
.BI \-a ", " \-\-artist " [QUERY]"
Filter by Artist. Opens the interactive Artist picker if
.I QUERY
is omitted. Supports OR aliases (e.g., \fB\-a "ado || natori"\fR).
.TP
.BI \-b ", " \-\-album " [QUERY]"
Filter by Album. Opens the interactive Album picker if
.I QUERY
is omitted. Supports OR aliases.
.TP
.BI \-g ", " \-\-genre " [QUERY]"
Filter by Genre. Opens the interactive Genre picker if
.I QUERY
is omitted. Supports OR aliases (e.g., \fB\-g "pop, rock"\fR).
.TP
.BI \-t ", " \-\-title " [QUERY]"
Filter by Track Title. Opens Track Mode if
.I QUERY
is omitted. Supports OR aliases.
.TP
.B \-\-or
Combine multiple filter flags using OR (union) instead of the default AND (intersection).
.TP
.BI \-l ", " \-\-playlist " [QUERY]"
Open Playlist Mode, or filter playlists if
.I QUERY
is provided.
.TP
.BI \-\-search " [QUERY]" "\fR, \fP" \-\-yt " [QUERY]"
Search YouTube directly for tracks and live streams (requires
.BR yt-dlp (1)).
.TP
.BI \-\-radio " [STATION]"
Open Radio Mode directly, or play a specific built-in station (e.g., \fBjpop\fR, \fBvocaloid\fR).
.SS "Playback & Audio"
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-play\-all
Play all matching tracks immediately without opening a disambiguation picker.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-shuffle
Enable shuffle playback for this session.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-shuffle
Disable shuffle playback for this session (preserves natural album/track ordering).
.TP
.BI \-\-loop " [MODE]"
Enable looping. Defaults to \fBinf\fR when passed without a value. Accepted values:
\fBinf\fR/\fBplaylist\fR/\fBall\fR, \fBtrack\fR/\fBfile\fR/\fBone\fR/\fBrepeat\fR,
\fBno\fR/\fBoff\fR/\fBfalse\fR, or a non-negative integer repeat count.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-loop
Disable all looping for this session.
.TP
.B \-\-repeat
Loop the currently playing track (Repeat One).
.TP
.BI \-\-gapless " [MODE]"
Configure gapless audio playback. Defaults to \fBtrue\fR when passed without a value.
Accepted values: \fBdefault\fR/\fBauto\fR/\fBweak\fR, \fBtrue\fR/\fByes\fR/\fBon\fR,
\fBfalse\fR/\fBno\fR/\fBoff\fR/\fBnone\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-gapless
Disable gapless playback for this session.
.TP
.BI \-\-replaygain " [MODE]"
Configure ReplayGain volume normalization. Defaults to \fBdefault\fR when passed without a value.
Accepted values: \fBdefault\fR/\fBauto\fR (uses \fBalbum\fR mode when shuffle is off in Album
or Directory Mode, and \fBtrack\fR mode otherwise), \fBalbum\fR, \fBtrack\fR,
or \fBno\fR/\fBoff\fR/\fBnone\fR/\fBfalse\fR. Enforces \fB\-\-replaygain\-clip=no\fR when active.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-replaygain
Disable ReplayGain volume normalization for this session.
.TP
.BI \-\-volume " LEVEL"
Set initial playback volume (0\(en100).
.TP
.B \-\-video\-ok
Include video files when browsing or playing.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-video
Force-disable video files (overrides \fIvideo_ok\fR in config).
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-watch
Play with the mpv video window enabled.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-watch
Force audio-only playback (overrides \fIwatch\fR in config).
.TP
.BI \-\-player " BIN"
Specify the player binary (defaults to \fBmpv\fR on Unix, \fBmpv.com\fR on Windows).
.TP
.BI \-\-ytdlp " BIN"
Specify the yt-dlp binary (defaults to \fByt-dlp\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-mpv\-args " ARGS..."
Pass extra raw arguments directly to
.BR mpv (1).
.SS "Configuration, Logs & Updates"
.TP
.BI \-c ", " \-\-config " [EDITOR]"
Open
.I config.toml
in \fIEDITOR\fR (falls back to \fB$EDITOR\fR, \fB$VISUAL\fR, or a system editor).
.TP
.BR \-\-remove\-config ", " \-\-rm\-conf
Delete \fIconfig.toml\fR to reset settings to defaults.
.TP
.BI \-\-log " [PAGER]"
View session log files.
.TP
.BI \-\-remove\-log " [COUNT]" "\fR, \fP" \-\-rm\-log " [COUNT]"
Delete all log files, or the oldest \fICOUNT\fR log files.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity (can be repeated).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable debug output.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-update
Check for and install application updates (available when built with the \fBupdate\fR feature).
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Auto-confirm the update prompt (available when built with the \fBupdate\fR feature).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print CLI help summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH SEARCH & OPERATORS
.B mpv-music
normalizes Unicode accents, case, full-width characters, and punctuation, tolerates
parenthetical tags (e.g., \fI(feat. ...)\fR, \fI[Remastered]\fR), and ranks exact and
word-boundary matches above fuzzy typos.
.PP
.TP
.B Unified Global Search
Positional queries search across Title, Artist, and Album simultaneously:
.br
\fBmpv-music "dean july"\fR
.TP
.B OR Union
Matches if any term matches. Supported operators: \fB||\fR, \fBOR\fR, \fB|\fR, \fB,\fR
.br
\fBmpv-music "natori || ado"\fR
.TP
.B AND Intersection
Matches only if all terms match. Supported operators: \fB&&\fR, \fBAND\fR, space, \fB;\fR
.br
\fBmpv-music "ado && miku"\fR
.TP
.B Flag OR Aliases & \-\-or
Individual filter flags accept OR aliases (\fB\-a "ado || eve" \-g "rock, pop"\fR).
Pass \fB\-\-or\fR to union results across separate filter flags instead of intersecting them.
.SH INTERACTIVE TUI
.SS "Main Menu Modes"
When launched with no arguments, the Main Menu provides:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDirectory Mode\fR \(em Browse folders (with pinned root \fImusic_dirs\fR) and play in natural track order.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBTrack Mode\fR \(em Fuzzy-search all indexed tracks with metadata & duration previews.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPlaylist Mode\fR \(em Select and queue \fI.m3u\fR/\fI.m3u8\fR/\fI.pls\fR playlists.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBTag Filter Mode\fR \(em Filter by Artist, Album, or Genre.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPlay All Mode\fR \(em Queue the entire indexed library.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSearch & Stream URL\fR \(em Search YouTube or stream a direct URL via \fByt\-dlp\fR(1).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRadio Mode\fR \(em Play curated built-in internet radio stations.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSettings\fR \(em Manage music directories, refresh/rebuild index, edit config, or clean logs.
.SS "Navigation & Selection Keys"
.TP
.B Type to filter
Fuzzy-filter the current list in real time (also supports \fB||\fR, \fBOR\fR, \fBAND\fR, \fB&&\fR, \fB,\fR).
.TP
.BR Up / Down ", " Ctrl+N / Ctrl+P
Move selection cursor.
.TP
.B TAB
Toggle multi-selection on the highlighted item.
.TP
.B Ctrl+A
Select all currently filtered items.
.TP
.B Ctrl+D
Deselect only the currently filtered items (clear the search bar first to deselect all, or press \fBAlt+D\fR).
.TP
.B Alt+D
Deselect all items unconditionally.
.TP
.B ENTER
Confirm selection and start playback (or enter the selected submenu).
.TP
.B ESC
Go back to the previous menu or exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is stored in TOML format in
.IR config.toml .
Run
.B mpv-music \-c
to edit it or
.B mpv-music \-\-remove\-config
to regenerate defaults.
.PP
Boolean and keyword fields accept standard TOML booleans as well as flexible string aliases:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBTrue aliases:\fR \fBtrue\fR, \fByes\fR, \fBon\fR, \fB"1"\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFalse aliases:\fR \fBfalse\fR, \fBno\fR, \fBoff\fR, \fBnone\fR, \fB"0"\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDefault aliases:\fR \fB"default"\fR, \fB"auto"\fR
.SS "Playback Settings"
.TP
.B shuffle
Type: \fIbool\fR. Default: \fBtrue\fR.
.br
Randomize playback order by default.
.TP
.B loop_mode
Type: \fIstring | bool | integer\fR. Default: \fB"inf"\fR.
.br
Accepted values: \fB"inf"\fR (\fB"playlist"\fR, \fB"all"\fR, \fBtrue\fR),
\fB"track"\fR (\fB"file"\fR, \fB"one"\fR, \fB"repeat"\fR),
\fB"no"\fR (\fB"off"\fR, \fB"none"\fR, \fBfalse\fR), or a non-negative integer count (e.g., \fB2\fR).
.TP
.B volume
Type: \fIinteger (0\(en130)\fR. Default: \fB100\fR.
.br
Initial mpv volume level (values above \fB130\fR are clamped to \fB100\fR on load).
.TP
.B gapless
Type: \fIstring | bool\fR. Default: \fB"default"\fR.
.br
Accepted values: \fB"default"\fR (\fB"auto"\fR, \fB"weak"\fR),
\fBtrue\fR (\fB"yes"\fR, \fB"on"\fR), or \fBfalse\fR (\fB"no"\fR, \fB"off"\fR, \fB"none"\fR).
.TP
.B replaygain
Type: \fIstring | bool\fR. Default: \fB"default"\fR.
.br
Accepted values: \fB"default"\fR (\fB"auto"\fR, \fBtrue\fR \(em context-aware \fBalbum\fR/\fBtrack\fR),
\fB"album"\fR, \fB"track"\fR, or \fB"no"\fR (\fB"off"\fR, \fB"none"\fR, \fBfalse\fR).
.SS "Library & Scanner Settings"
.TP
.B music_dirs
Type: \fIarray of paths\fR. Default: system audio directory (e.g., \fB["~/Music"]\fR).
.br
List of root directories scanned during indexing.
.TP
.B video_ok
Type: \fIbool\fR. Default: \fBfalse\fR.
.br
Include video extensions when indexing and browsing.
.TP
.B watch
Type: \fIbool\fR. Default: \fBfalse\fR.
.br
Enable mpv video window during playback.
.TP
.B scan_hidden_dirs
Type: \fIbool\fR. Default: \fBfalse\fR.
.br
Traverse hidden directories (starting with \fB.\fR) when indexing.
.TP
.B serial_mode
Type: \fIbool\fR. Default: \fBfalse\fR.
.br
Disable parallel scanning and process files on a single thread.
.TP
.B filename_pattern
Type: \fIstring\fR. Default: \fB"default"\fR.
.br
Fallback metadata template used when audio tags are missing. Supports
\fB{artist}\fR, \fB{title}\fR, \fB{album}\fR, and \fB{track}\fR tokens
(e.g., \fB"{track} - {artist} - {title}"\fR). Set to \fB"default"\fR for built-in heuristics.
.TP
.B audio_exts\fR, \fBvideo_exts\fR, \fBplaylist_exts
Type: \fIarray of strings\fR. Default: \fB["default"]\fR.
.br
File extensions recognized by the indexer. Include \fB"default"\fR to inherit the built-in
list, add custom extensions (e.g., \fB"TAK"\fR), or exclude specific built-in extensions
using \fB"!"\fR or \fB"-"\fR prefixes (e.g., \fB["default", "!amr", "dsd"]\fR).
Built-in defaults:
.br
\(bu \fIaudio_exts\fR: mp3, flac, wav, m4a, aac, ogg, opus, wma, alac, aiff, aif, amr, ape, dsf, mpc, wv, spx
.br
\(bu \fIvideo_exts\fR: mp4, mkv, webm, avi, mov, flv, wmv, mpeg, mpg, 3gp, ts, vob, m4v
.br
\(bu \fIplaylist_exts\fR: m3u, m3u8, pls
.SS "UI, Logging & External Tools"
.TP
.B nerd_fonts
Type: \fIstring | bool\fR. Default: \fB"none"\fR.
.br
Accepted values: \fB"none"\fR (\fB"default"\fR, \fB"auto"\fR, \fBfalse\fR),
\fB"mono"\fR (\fBtrue\fR, \fB"yes"\fR, \fB"on"\fR), or
\fB"normal"\fR (\fB"symbols"\fR, \fB"prop"\fR, \fB"propo"\fR).
.TP
.B player
Type: \fIstring\fR. Default: \fB"mpv"\fR.
.br
Player executable name or path (\fB"default"\fR resolves to \fBmpv\fR / \fBmpv.com\fR).
.TP
.B mpv_args
Type: \fIarray of strings\fR. Default: \fB[]\fR.
.br
Extra arguments appended to every mpv invocation (legacy key \fImpv_default_args\fR is migrated automatically).
.TP
.B ytdlp
Type: \fIstring\fR. Default: \fB"yt-dlp"\fR.
.br
yt-dlp executable name or path (\fB"default"\fR resolves to \fByt-dlp\fR).
.TP
.B ytdlp_useragent
Type: \fIstring\fR. Default: \fB"default"\fR.
.br
HTTP User-Agent passed to yt-dlp (\fB"default"\fR uses the built-in Firefox User-Agent).
.TP
.B ytdlp_ejs_remote_github
Type: \fIbool\fR. Default: \fBfalse\fR.
.br
Allow yt-dlp to fetch remote EJS components from GitHub.
.TP
.B enable_file_logging
Type: \fIbool\fR. Default: \fBtrue\fR.
.br
Write session logs to the state directory.
.TP
.B max_log_sessions
Type: \fIinteger (>= 1)\fR. Default: \fB3\fR.
.br
Maximum number of recent log files retained on disk (\fB0\fR is reset to \fB1\fR on load).
.SS "Example config.toml"
.nf
.RS 4
shuffle = true
loop_mode = "inf"
volume = 100
gapless = "default"
replaygain = "default"
nerd_fonts = "mono"
music_dirs = ["/home/user/Music"]
audio_exts = ["default", "!amr"]
filename_pattern = "default"
mpv_args = []
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
Paths follow platform XDG/standard conventions:
.TP
.I ~/.config/mpv-music/config.toml
Main TOML configuration file (on macOS: \fI~/Library/Application Support/com.furqanhun.mpv-music/config.toml\fR;
on Windows: \fI%APPDATA%\\furqanhun\\mpv-music\\config\\config.toml\fR).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/mpv-music/music_index.jsonl
Indexed track metadata database.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/mpv-music/yt_cache.json
Cached YouTube search metadata.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/mpv-music/logs/
Session log files (falls back to the data directory if no state directory is defined).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Launch the interactive TUI:
.B mpv-music
.TP
Play a specific album or artist via unified search:
.B mpv-music "currents"
.TP
Search with OR / AND operators and play immediately without a picker:
.B mpv-music "ado || natori" \-p
.TP
Filter by multiple genres and artists using union (\-\-or):
.B mpv-music \-a ado \-g "j-pop, rock" \-\-or
.TP
Play an album folder in natural track order with album ReplayGain:
.B mpv-music \-\-no\-shuffle /path/to/album
.TP
Search YouTube for a track or live stream:
.B mpv-music \-\-yt "lofi hip hop"
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpv (1),
.BR yt-dlp (1)
.PP
Project homepage and documentation:
.I https://furqanhun.github.io/mpv-music/
